detectDateFormat←{
    ⍝ 1 if the dates in schedule text ⍵ are DD/MM/YYYY, 0 if MM/DD/YYYY:
    ⍝ whichever reading gives a real date for every one of them.
    dates←'\b\d{1,2}/\d{1,2}/\d{4}\b'⎕S'&'⊢⍵

    ⍝ Return early if no dates found
    0=≢dates:'NO_DATES'⎕SIGNAL 100

    ⍝ ⎕DT validate mode (target 0): 1 for each real date, 0 for month 13, 31 February, ...
    mmdd ddmm←{∧/(⍵ 0)⎕DT dates}¨'M/D/YYYY' 'D/M/YYYY'

    ⍝ Both readings work: no date has a day after the 12th
    ddmm∧mmdd:'AMBIGUOUS'⎕SIGNAL 100

    ddmm:1
    mmdd:0

    ⍝ Neither works: the dates are a mix of both formats, or impossible
    'INCONSISTENT Dates'⎕SIGNAL 100
}
